gaG7(){return"Internal Rate of Return (IRR) \u2014 your personal annualised return, adjusted for the exact timing of every buy and sell.\n\nUnlike simple P/L%, IRR accounts for how long each amount was invested. A 20% IRR means your money grew at 20% per year on average.\n\nAccounts for the exact timing and size of every cash flow in your portfolio."},
gaG8(){return"Your annualised return accounting for when each investment was made."},
gaG9(){return"Add owned stocks to see position sizes."},
gaGa(){return"Shows how concentrated your portfolio is and how much dry powder you have.\n\n\u2022 Position sizes \u2014 each stock as a % of total portfolio value\n\u2022 Cash / Liquidity \u2014 uninvested cash you can deploy\n\nLarge single positions increase risk. A cash buffer lets you act on opportunities.\n\nWhat your cash affects: it counts toward your Total wealth and your concentration % (it shows as a slice here), and nothing else. It does NOT change your returns (IRR), risk metrics (VaR, Sharpe, beta) or the equity curve \u2014 those are based on your holdings only."},
aGb(a,b,c){return"Lens: your own closed rounds with your own thresholds \u2014 win \u2265 "+c+", loss \u2264 "+b+", floor "+a+" rounds per trait. Verdicts are tendencies computed by rule, not grades, and never buy or sell advice."},
gaGd(){return"Profitability"},
gaGc(){return"Profit on everything you put in, including the cash you got back from sells & dividends."},
gaGe(){return"A snapshot of your portfolio's fundamental characteristics.\n\n\u2022 Company Size \u2014 market cap buckets (Mega/Large/Mid/Small Cap)\n\u2022 Workforce Scale \u2014 employee headcount per stock\n\u2022 Valuation \u2014 simple average P/E vs market norms (see the value-weighted P/E in By Asset Class)\n\u2022 Income \u2014 dividend yield distribution\n\u2022 Profitability \u2014 profit margin range across holdings"},
aGf(a){return"\u03b2 "+a+" (excluded)"},
gaGg(){return"Biggest Winners"},
gaGh(){return'Biggest Winners \u2014 P/L% \xd7 position weight\n\nCombines how well a stock performed with how much of your shown portfolio it represents.\nA +40% gain on 20% of your portfolio outranks a +40% gain on 2%.\n\nWeight is each holding\'s value in your display currency, relative to the stocks currently shown (tag filter affects this). A holding with no exchange rate is left out and shows "no rate".'},
gaGi(){return"Compounding"},
gaGj(){return"Compounding Quality \u2014 Annualised return (CAGR)\n\nHow fast each position compounds per year.\nRequires at least 90 days of holding \u2014 newer positions sort to the bottom."},
aGk(a){return"  \xb7  "+a+" div"},
gaGl(){return'Income Score \u2014 Dividends on the shares you still hold \xf7 Cost of those shares \xd7 100\n\nHow much income your current position has generated relative to what you put in.\nDividends earned by shares you have since sold are not in the score (the amount shown is everything received).\nStocks with no dividends logged score 0.\nStocks with no investment recorded sort to the bottom, and so does a stock with a dividend whose exchange rate has not arrived yet (it shows "\u2014").'},
